# r1113 Power Grid boot on jar jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-16.jar (sha1 618ed8016949, port
# phase 9.4: all of -15 (P9b, P9c) plus P9d: Integrated Circuit, boost recipes, electrical gizmo assembly; fixes B27 to
# B29). Supersedes pwg15.qb (the -15 boot ran with broken probes: perf/runs/r1113/verdicts/pwg15.md). One boot, one
# batch, this order:
#   1. SQ-PWG-84 boot row (version 19.2-16, phase 9.4, ns counts, 106 recipes, zpwg9b / 9c / 9d check)
#   2. SQ-PWG-72 P9b boot part (registries, menus, packets, zpwg9 check incl. the SQ-PWG-67 tag line, reload)
#   3. SQ-PWG-57 rerun for fix B20 (passed in pwg15: FE gained 20000 = charge lost 20000; kept as a regression)
#   4. P9b rows SQ-PWG-73, -74, -75; P9c rows SQ-PWG-76 (P9c part), SETUP15, -77 to -83 (as pwg15, fixed probes)
#   5. P9d rows SQ-PWG-85 to -89 (queue run order; CQ-PWG-27 is a client row, not here)
#   6. SQ-PWG-63 rerun with the p8 `use hit loc=` print (pwg12r verdict), at pwg12r's spot X 1300
#   SQ-PWG-67's tag check is not a separate row: SQ-PWG-72 runs `zpwg9 check`, whose `missing=[...]` line already
#   answered it in pwg15 (missing=[create:copper_nugget]: the pack removes that item, Creative Common removed_items.js).
# Group A superflat, level pwg16, spawn-animals=true, ground Y -61 (grass), blocks at Y -60. Each area's SETUP row kills
# the animals generated in its chunks (box selector) and SETUP14A stops mob spawning.
# Areas (no block overlap):
#   P9d   X 1095 to 1200, Z 1920 to 1990 (SQ-PWG-84 forceload; -85 Z 1929 to 1940 X 1102 to 1114, -86 fake player 1120 1930,
#         -87 Z 1947 to 1957, -88 Z 1963 to 1976, -89 Z 1984 to 1985 X 1102 to 1112)
#   P9b   X 1090 to 1130, Z 1805 to 1850 (SQ-PWG-72 forceload; -73 Z 1810 to 1825, -74 / -75 Z 1820 to 1835)
#   P7    X 1095 to 1115, Z 1535 to 1545 (SETUP14P7; SQ-PWG-57's fake player at 1100 -60 1540, no blocks)
#   P9c   X 1135 to 1200, Z 1855 to 1915 (SQ-PWG-76 forceload; as pwg15.qb)
#   P8    X 1290 to 1320, Z 1590 to 1615 (SETUP63; SQ-PWG-63 Z 1598 to 1609)
# Prep (INST = the instance root; all before the boot):
#   COPYDEV=1 PGJAR=$INST/jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-16.jar prep_srv.sh OUT pwg16 A spawn-animals=true
#   ls OUT/srv/mods | grep -i -E 'powergrid|cc-tweaked'   (only backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-16.jar: remove -15 and
#     older; cc-tweaked-1.19.2-1.101.4.jar present); sha1sum of the jar starts 618ed8016949
#   for p in pwg_probe pwg_grid_probe pwg_p3_probe pwg_p4_probe pwg_p5_probe pwg_p6_probe pwg_p7_probe pwg_p8_probe pwg_p9a_probe pwg_p9b_probe pwg_p9c_probe pwg_p9d_probe; do
#     cp $INST/tools/scratch_query/$p.js OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_$p.js; done      (twelve probes, the CURRENT copies:
#     p9b loads without io.netty (packets applied as built, bytes=none); p9c: acid by registry id, absMoveTo rotation,
#     deployer property axis_along_first, motors placed before their machines, basin / spout fill by tank NBT; p9d:
#     no getClass, signature calls for RecipeApplier and BoostRecipe.matches, ItemStack.finishUsingItem(level, player),
#     absMoveTo fake player, unbreaking read from NBT)
#   grep -c 'const $Unpooled' OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_pwg_p9b_probe.js   (0: the netty load is optional, in a try)
#   ponder datapack from the -16 jar (77 structure files; SQ-PWG-72 checks it is enabled, no row places from it):
#   rm -rf OUT/pwgp; mkdir -p OUT/pwgp OUT/srv/pwg16/datapacks/pwgponder/data/pwgponder/structures \
#     && unzip -o -q OUT/srv/mods/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-16.jar 'assets/powergrid/ponder/*' -d OUT/pwgp \
#     && cp -r OUT/pwgp/assets/powergrid/ponder/. OUT/srv/pwg16/datapacks/pwgponder/data/pwgponder/structures/ \
#     && printf '{"pack":{"pack_format":10,"description":"PWG ponder structures, scratch only"}}' > OUT/srv/pwg16/datapacks/pwgponder/pack.mcmeta
#   find OUT/srv/pwg16/datapacks/pwgponder -name '*.nbt' | wc -l      (77)
#   Loading Protection (shorter protection window, as pwg10 / pwg12 / pwg15):
#   python3 $INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py toml OUT/srv/config/loadingprotection-common.toml '"Loading Protection Configuration"' protectionDuration 1
#   Nothing else: no CC program or CC startup copy (no SQ-PWG-66-like row), no other datapack, no config edit.
# Run: qrun.py run OUT tools/scratch_query/batches/r1113/pwg16.qb perf/runs/r1113/pwg16
# Probe goggle reads log a RuntimeDistCleaner ERROR (client class): no blanket ERROR reject.
# waitlog matches anywhere since the row start; real waits are sleeps (20 ticks = 1 s) plus pace (s after each command).
# Batch deviations from the row text: as pwg15.qb for SQ-PWG-57 and -73 to -83 (tick waits are sleeps; CONSUME
# accepted beside SUCCESS; MCA villagers accepted as \S*villager\S*; SQ-PWG-83 does not branch on a byproduct); SQ-PWG-72
# accepts the circuit_component tag at 27 with missing=[create:copper_nugget] (pack removal); SQ-PWG-73 accepts
# bytes=none; SQ-PWG-80 checks the two basin tanks in either order; SQ-PWG-85 waits 120 / 200 ticks as 6 / 10 s sleeps;
# SQ-PWG-86 counts the chip uses (5 using=true, 6 using=false incl. the pickaxe and the four "again" uses); SQ-PWG-88
# checks the MCA villagers by health deltas from 20 (look if their max health is not 20); SQ-PWG-89 waits up to 200 s
# for "loop done" (a byproduct ends it LOOK: rerun with --rows SQ-PWG-89 after moving Z).
pace 1

